  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.pepperdine.edu/pepperdine-jobs": {
      "title": "PEPPERDINE UNIVERSITY CAREERS",
      "description": "Homepage Home Staff Opportunities Featured Careers Department of Facilities Services Rotational Program Temporary Opportunities Public Safety College of Health Science Why Pepperdine View All Jobs Applicant Login My Settings Kiosk mode PEPPERDINE UNIVERSITY CAREERS Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Staff Faculty Dining and Hospitality Student Recently Posted Jobs Title Major Area Summary Program Manager, Youth Leadership Initiatives SVP Strategic Implementation The Youth Leadership Initiative (YLI), which is part of the Office of Church Relations, is dedicated to raising up the next generation of Christian leaders. Through various projects and events, the initiative provides youth across America with resources and training to develop the skills necessary for pursuing lives of leadership, committed to Christ.\n\nThis position would be responsible for assisting the YLI director in the administration of events, communications and fundraising. They will aid in building bridges through networking with leaders in Churches of Christ and Restoration churches as well as prospective students from those churches. They will also oversee and train student workers who serve in the CrossWays Christian leadership training event as well as student workers in the Church Relations office. Manager, Enterprise Constituent Relationship Management Information Technology Under the guidance of the Senior Director of Enterprise CRM, the Manager leads the operational support and implementation of the University's Enterprise CRM Solutions. This leader ensures that Salesforce solutions effectively support Admissions, Recruitment, Advancement, Outreach, and Marketing by managing project assignments, coordinating technical and operational staff, and aligning technology with business strategies across diverse schools and units. Office Coordinator, Planned Giving Advancement The Office Coordinator oversees the day-to-day operations of Advancement’s Planned Giving team, assists in outreach, marketing, and event planning efforts, and provides administrative support to planned giving staff, all while maintaining a professional level of attention to detail, accuracy, timeliness, confidentiality, and discretion. Temporary Finance Support Liaison (Part-Time) Finance This position will support Pepperdine’s Finance Department in supporting University-wide adherence to Pepperdine’s University Financial Policies and support the Controllership Team with logistical and procedural needs. Adjunct Faculty Pool: School of Physician Assistant Studies College of Health Science Pepperdine University School of Physician Assistant Studies invites applications for Adjunct Faculty appointments to support its developing* graduate Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies (MSPAS) Program. Adjunct faculty play a vital role in preparing future Physician Assistants (PA) through high-quality instructional experiences that support student learning, clinical reasoning, professional development, and readiness for clinical practice.\n\nThe MSPAS Program seeks candidates who are committed to excellence in PA education and student development. Pepperdine Careers 24255 Pacific Coast Highway Malibu, CA 90263 310.506.4397 Quick Links Home Staff Opportunities Why Pepperdine Hiring Process Applicant Login My Settings Copyright © 2026 Pepperdine University Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
