    "https://jobs.pepperdine.edu/jobs/search/public-safety": {
      "title": "Department of Public Safety",
      "description": "Department of Public Safety Home Staff Opportunities Featured Careers Department of Facilities Services Rotational Program Temporary Opportunities Public Safety College of Health Science Why Pepperdine View All Jobs Applicant Login My Settings Kiosk mode Department of Public Safety About Pepperdine Why Work at Pepperdine? Hiring Process FAQ Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 1 filter options found Category Campus Security/Safety (3 items) 3 Employment Type Search employment types 1 filter options found Employment Type Regular (3 items) 3 City Search cities 1 filter options found City Malibu Campus (3 items) 3 Major Area Search 1 filter options found Major Area Department of Public Safety (3 items) 3 Employment Category Search 1 filter options found Employment Category Staff (3 items) 3 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Campus Safety Dispatcher Malibu Campus Campus Security/Safety Regular Department of Public Safety Staff The Department of Public Safety at Pepperdine University maintains a hospitable and secure campus environment while respecting the rights and dignity of each individual, in line with the University’s Christian mission. Through prompt and courteous communication, monitoring of systems, and use of sound judgment, Communications Officers play a critical role in creating and maintaining a welcoming, respectful, safe, and peaceful campus community. Read more Booth Officer Malibu Campus Campus Security/Safety Regular Department of Public Safety Staff The Booth Officer will play a critical role in welcoming faculty, staff, students, and visitors to campus while also identifying, assessing, and mitigating potential security threats at our campus entrances. The Department of Public Safety at Pepperdine University maintains a hospitable and secure campus environment while respecting the rights and dignity of each individual, in line with the University’s Christian mission. Through education, enforcement, emergency response, and 24/7 services, Public Safety Officers play a critical role in creating and maintaining a welcoming, respectful, safe, and peaceful campus community. Read more Lieutenant Malibu Campus Campus Security/Safety Regular Department of Public Safety Staff Under the supervision of the Captain of Public Safety, the Lieutenant is responsible for overseeing patrol operations within the Department of Public Safety, which includes, but is not limited to, the following responsibilities: leadership and daily supervision to all field supervisors, patrol officers, and booth officers, providing field operational support, serving as acting watch commander and admin on duty while on campus, reviewing reports for accuracy and to provide training/feedback to personnel to further\ntheir development, referring reports needing further follow-up to investigations, and executing training plans for patrol personnel. Read more Displaying all 3 entries Pepperdine Careers 24255 Pacific Coast Highway Malibu, CA 90263 310.506.4397 Quick Links Home Staff Opportunities Why Pepperdine Hiring Process Applicant Login My Settings Copyright © 2026 Pepperdine University Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources 