    "https://jobs.pepperdine.edu/faq": {
      "title": "Hiring Process",
      "description": "FAQ Home Staff Opportunities Featured Careers Department of Facilities Services Rotational Program Temporary Opportunities Public Safety College of Health Science Why Pepperdine View All Jobs Applicant Login My Settings Kiosk mode Hiring Process Frequently Asked Questions I applied for a position and haven't heard back. What is the status of my application? At Pepperdine, we have a decentralized recruitment process, meaning each position has its own hiring manager and departments directly complete the recruitment process for that position. You will hear directly from the department regarding any next steps. Can I apply for multiple positions? Yes. You may apply to as many positions as you would like and manage your applications under one applicant account. How long does the hiring process take? The hiring process varies in length depending on the position and the applicant pool. How do I know if the job is still accepting applications? All posted jobs are in active recruitment and accepting new applications. What are restricted positions? Restricted positions can be compared with regular positions as follows: Benefits : Regular and restricted positions qualify for the same type and level of University benefits. Renewal cycle: Restricted positions have an expected end date. In order to renew the position beyond this date, the position must be evaluated to determine whether funding exists. Not a contract: Restricted positions, along with regular positions, are at-will employment. Although restricted positions have an expected end date, this does not represent a contract term. The position may be ended at any time, and there is no guarantee of continued employment after the current restricted position ends. Performance expectations: Performance expectations for restricted positions are the same as those for regular staff positions. Accordingly, all performance expectations of a restricted position must be met to be successful in the position. What benefits does Pepperdine offer? To learn about Pepperdine's competitive benefits offerings and eligibility requirements, please review the Staff and Faculty Benefits website. How do I find out about new job openings? If you are interested in working at Pepperdine but do not see a job currently posted relevant to your skills and experience, you can sign up for Job Alerts to receive updates based on your criteria, or contact Human Resources at employment@pepperdine.edu for additional information. Can I make updates to my personal information and resume after I submit my application? Yes. You may make updates to your personal information and upload a revised resume at any time through your applicant account. However, you are unable to make changes to job-specific application questions once your application is submitted. If you have additional questions, please contact employment@pepperdine.edu . Pepperdine Careers 24255 Pacific Coast Highway Malibu, CA 90263 310.506.4397 Quick Links Home Staff Opportunities Why Pepperdine Hiring Process Applicant Login My Settings Copyright © 2026 Pepperdine University Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
    },
    "https://jobs.pepperdine.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-pool-school-of-physician-assistant-studies-calabasas-campus-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Pool: School of Physician Assistant Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Pool: School of Physician Assistant Studies - Calabasas Campus, California, United States Home Staff Opportunities Featured Careers Department of Facilities Services Rotational Program Temporary Opportunities Public Safety College of Health Science Why Pepperdine View All Jobs Applicant Login My Settings Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty Pool: School of Physician Assistant Studies College of Health Science Adjunct Faculty Pool: School of Physician Assistant Studies Calabasas Campus Health Care Adjunct College of Health Science Add to favorites View favorites Pepperdine University School of Physician Assistant Studies invites applications for Adjunct Faculty appointments to support its developing* graduate Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies (MSPAS) Program. Adjunct faculty play a vital role in preparing future Physician Assistants (PA) through high-quality instructional experiences that support student learning, clinical reasoning, professional development, and readiness for clinical practice. The MSPAS Program seeks candidates who are committed to excellence in PA education and student development. Adjunct Faculty Responsibilities: Adjunct faculty may be assigned instructional responsibilities based on program needs and individual qualifications. Responsibilities may include: Provide instruction to PA students. Supporting student achievement of course learning outcomes and program competencies. Facilitate the development of clinical reasoning, professional identity, and safe patient care practices. Participating in lectures, laboratory instruction, clinical skills instruction, small-group facilitation, case-based learning, simulation activities, OSCEs, practical assessments, or other instructional activities as assigned. Evaluate student performance using established rubrics, evaluation tools and program standards. Participating in program committees as assigned. Maintain compliance with Program and University policies. Communicate regularly with program faculty and leadership to support student success. Uphold a supportive, structured, and professional learning environment. Faculty Expectations Adjunct Faculty are expected to: Be present for all assigned instructional responsibilities. Prepare for assigned teaching activities in advance. Coordinate any unforeseen absences in advance with course leadership, with appropriate coverage to maintain uninterrupted student instruction. Communicate student concerns, performance issues, or professionalism concerns to course leadership in a timely manner. Course directors maintain scheduled office hours. Model professional and ethical behavior consistent with the expectations of the PA Program and Pepperdine University. Acceptance of an Adjunct Faculty appointment signifies a commitment to fulfill assigned instructional responsibilities. Failure to meet these expectations may result in reassignment or withdrawal of the appointment. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Master’s degree or doctoral degree from a nationally accredited college or university. Minimum of one year of clinical or professional experience. Professional licensure, certification, or specialty certification. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in teaching, precepting, or mentoring PA students or other health professions students. Clinical expertise aligned with PA program instructional needs, such as anatomy, biomedical science, clinical medicine, clinical reasoning, pharmacology, medical-surgical content, behavioral and mental health, women’s health, pediatrics, emergency medicine, procedural skills, or other areas of PA practice. Experience with simulation, skills instruction, OSCEs, practical assessments, or clinical evaluation tools. Experience supporting student learning in a structured academic or clinical education environment. The ideal candidates will: Demonstrate a commitment to student-centered teaching and mentorship. Model professionalism, ethical behavior, humility, service, and respect. Engage effectively with interdisciplinary teams. Support the mission and values of Pepperdine University and the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies. Application Instructions Please submit all application materials to: https://apply.interfolio.com/190221 Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter addressing: Clinical, professional, teaching, or subject matter experience Areas of clinical or subject matter expertise Contact information for two professional references Professional license(s) and certification(s), as applicable Questions about the application process can be directed to: Dr. Amy Bronson (amy.bronson@pepperdine.edu) Founding Dean, School of Physician Assistant Studies Program Director, Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies Pepperdine University 24255 Pacific Coast Highway Malibu, CA 902633 Qualified individuals should be able to show respect for workplace differences, and have the ability to work effectively with individuals from different backgrounds. Offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a criminal, education, and employment screening to include official transcripts. The University conducts such screenings in compliance with applicable laws and with the objectives of evaluating risk and supporting a safe environment for students, faculty, staff, and guests; safeguarding key University assets including people, property, information, and the University’s reputation; and providing comprehensive job-related information to University leaders to enable them to make prudent hiring decisions. Qualified individuals with criminal histories will be considered for employment in compliance with applicable laws, including the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance. This is an Adjunct, Exempt position with multiple openings. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling, as-needed basis. Appointments vary based on enrollment, curricular needs, course assignments, and program requirements. Expected Pay Range: $2,370 per unit The above pay range reflects what Pepperdine University reasonably expects to pay for this position at time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on relevant factors such as work experience, market conditions, education/training, and skill level. Pepperdine is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of any status or condition protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. Pepperdine is committed to providing a work environment free from all forms of unlawful discrimination and harassment. Engaging in unlawful discrimination or harassment will result in appropriate disciplinary action, up to and including dismissal from the University. Pepperdine is religiously affiliated with the Churches of Christ. It is the purpose of Pepperdine to pursue the very highest employment and academic standards within a context that celebrates and extends the spiritual and ethical ideals of the Christian faith. While students, faculty, and staff represent many religious backgrounds, Pepperdine is permitted under applicable law and reserves the right to seek, hire, and promote persons who support the goals and mission of the institution, including the right to prefer co-religionists who support Pepperdine's Christian mission. *Pepperdine University, Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies (MSPAS) has applied for Accreditation - Provisional from the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant (ARC-PA). The MSPAS program anticipates matriculating its first class in September 2027 pending achieving Accreditation - Provisional status at the April 2027 ARC-PA meeting. Accreditation - Provisional is an accreditation status granted when the plans and resource allocation, if fully implemented as planned, of a proposed program that has not yet enrolled students appear to demonstrate the program’s ability to meet the ARC-PA Standards or when a program holding Accreditation - Provisional status appears to demonstrate continued progress in complying with the Standards as it prepares for the graduation of the first class (cohort) of students. If the MSPAS Program does not achieve Accreditation - Provisional status, the program will not commence, and students will not matriculate. Accepted students will be refunded for any deposits or tuition paid. Application fees are not refundable. The MSPAS Program at Pepperdine University has been approved by the Western Association of Schools and Colleges (WASC) Senior College & University Commission (WSCUC). Recommended Jobs Program Manager, Youth Leadership Initiatives Malibu Campus Manager, Enterprise Constituent Relationship Management Remote Pepperdine Careers 24255 Pacific Coast Highway Malibu, CA 90263 310.506.4397 Quick Links Home Staff Opportunities Why Pepperdine Hiring Process Applicant Login My Settings Copyright © 2026 Pepperdine University Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
