    "https://jobs.pepperdine.edu/jobs/visiting-assistant-professor-of-management-malibu-campus-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Management",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Management - Malibu Campus, California, United States Home Staff Opportunities Featured Careers Department of Facilities Services Rotational Program Temporary Opportunities Public Safety College of Health Science Why Pepperdine View All Jobs Applicant Login My Settings Kiosk mode Visiting Assistant Professor of Management Seaver College Visiting Assistant Professor of Management Malibu Campus Teaching Full-Time Seaver College Add to favorites View favorites The Business Administration Division of the Seaver College of Letters, Arts, and Sciences at Pepperdine University seeks a candidate with an earned Ph.D. in organizational behavior, management, or a closely related field for a visiting position which begins August 1, 2027. The primary teaching responsibility will be in organizational behavior; however, the ability to teach other courses such as management theory and practice and strategic management would be highly desirable. Candidates are expected to complete all requirements for the Ph.D. before the date of appointment. A strong candidate who is ABD would be considered. A documented research interest in organizational behavior or a management-related field is required, and teaching experience is preferred. The business program at Seaver College is accredited by AACSB and we have approximately 1,000 undergraduate students in the Business Administration Division. The division is student-centric; our classes are small (rarely more than 35 students) and our faculty is collegial and collaborative. The division offers Bachelor of Science degree programs in accounting, business administration, finance, and international business and several minors. All degree programs are offered on a full-time, residential basis at the main campus in Malibu, California. Seaver College has an enrollment of approximately 3,500 students. Please visit our website for more information. Pepperdine University was established in 1937 by Mr. George Pepperdine, a Christian businessman, who stressed the desirability of a holistic education built on Christian principles. The institution is committed to the ideals of the founder. Successful candidates must demonstrate an active commitment to the Christian mission of the University and the mission of Seaver College . Located near Los Angeles in Southern California, Pepperdine University is especially interested in candidates who can contribute through their teaching, research, and service to the excellence of the University and our surrounding community. The salary for this appointment will range from $121,000 - $135,000 per year and reflects what Pepperdine University reasonably expects to pay for a visiting appointment based on the qualifications and experience of the applicant. In addition to salary, Pepperdine offers a robust suite of employee benefits . Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please submit all application materials to https://apply.interfolio.com/190999. Qualified individuals should be able to show respect for workplace differences, and have the ability to work effectively with individuals from different backgrounds. Offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a criminal, education, and employment screening. The University conducts such screenings in compliance with applicable laws and with the objectives of evaluating risk and supporting a safe environment for students, faculty, staff, and guests; safeguarding key University assets including people, property, information, and the University’s reputation; and providing comprehensive job-related information to University leaders to enable them to make prudent hiring decisions. Qualified individuals with criminal histories will be considered for employment in compliance with applicable laws, including the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance. For more information, please contact the chair of the search committee: Dr. Chris Collins (christopher.collins@pepperdine.edu) Associate Professor of Management and Organizational Behavior Application Instructions Applications should include the documents listed below: A cover letter . A curriculum vitae , indicating educational record, employment record, achievements, awards, publications, and other relevant information. Please also describe any civic, religious, or charitable interests and activities, and list all current organizational memberships. Three confidential letters of reference (an email address for each referral will be requested in the application). Official transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial copies are acceptable for the application; however, official transcripts will be required for selected applicants). Personal Statement . Reflect on Pepperdine’s Christian mission and address your pattern of support for generally accepted Christian values and the University’s mission, your active participation in a faith community, and your practice or vision for integrating faith and learning in the classroom. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Pepperdine is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of any status or condition protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. Pepperdine is committed to providing a work environment free from all forms of unlawful discrimination and harassment. Engaging in unlawful discrimination or harassment will result in appropriate disciplinary action, up to and including dismissal from the University. Pepperdine is religiously affiliated with the Churches of Christ. It is the purpose of Pepperdine to pursue the very highest employment and academic standards within a context that celebrates and extends the spiritual and ethical ideals of the Christian faith. While students, faculty, and staff represent many religious backgrounds, Pepperdine is permitted under applicable law and reserves the right to seek, hire and promote persons who support the goals and mission of the institution, including the right to prefer co-religionists who support Pepperdine's Christian mission. Recommended Jobs Program Manager, Youth Leadership Initiatives Malibu Campus Manager, Enterprise Constituent Relationship Management Remote Pepperdine Careers 24255 Pacific Coast Highway Malibu, CA 90263 310.506.4397 Quick Links Home Staff Opportunities Why Pepperdine Hiring Process Applicant Login My Settings Copyright © 2026 Pepperdine University Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
